resources.string:
A test tool for the Spoiler Blocker project. While it is on, it:

• reads the layout of whichever app is in front, and draws a coloured box over one list item to measure how well the box keeps up with scrolling;
• notes the time of every touch on the screen (the time only, not what was touched) and, for ten seconds when asked, takes over touch input to test whether Android passes it on;
• takes a screenshot of the app in front, only when asked, and saves it in this app's private storage;
• saves the text and layout of the screen in front, only when asked, in this app's private storage;
• writes a line to its private log every minute to show that it is still running.

Nothing leaves the phone. Screen text is stored only in the dumps you ask for. Turn the service off when the experiments are finished.
